unit: dm-vocab-compile-fail-test
commits: 441e28534 (the compile-fail suite, watched red)
what: ADD corpus-engine-vocab/tests/atoms_reds.rs, the trybuild suite O8 step 2
  describes (the `nc-thesis` shape), pinning that an `AtomsFile` built outside
  `vocab::read` cannot yield atoms. Two fixtures, one per construction DM §10.5
  "The correction" names as the door — `serde_json::from_str::<AtomsFile>` (the
  derived `Deserialize`, atoms.rs:1527) and the struct literal (both fields
  `pub`, atoms.rs:1529-1530) — plus tests/ui/harness_positive_control.rs, which
  always fails to compile and gates the reading. `trybuild` is a dev-dep, so the
  leaf's shipped closure is unchanged (boundary_gate.rs:577 ignores dev edges);
  Cargo.lock gains only the corpus-engine-vocab -> trybuild edge. Watched red
  first (O8 step 2): with both fixtures asserted `compile_fail` the suite
  reports "Expected test case to fail to compile, but it succeeded" for each —
  the illegal construction compiles today, which is the red. The committed
  polarity is `t.pass` (a red suite is not a gate, §5, and
  TEST(corpus-engine-vocab) is this row's check); REVIEW-build-vocab-seal flips
  both to `compile_fail` when it seals the type and records the `.stderr` then.
checks: CLEAN exit=0 (disk gate, cache kept); LINT exit=0 (7 crates, errors: 0);
  TEST(corpus-engine-vocab) exit=0 (54 pass, 0 fail); BOUNDARY exit=0
  (corpus-engine-vocab still a package_leaf, 34 crates). Red observed: 2 of 3
  fixtures "Expected test case to fail to compile, but it succeeded" under the
  temporary compile_fail polarity.
